udolf Harbig"] ", set in 1939. The other great race that year came at the Pan-American Games when " [:a {:href "/athletes/79074"} "Arnie Sowell"] " (USA) defeated his countryman, " [:a {:href "/athletes/79084"} "Lon Spurrier"] ". Sowell was AAU Champion in 1955-56, but American " [:a {:href "/athletes/78270"} "Tom Courtney"] " was probably a slight favorite in Melbourne, having won the US Olympic Trials. Moens could not compete, having injured his knee a few months before the Olympics. In the Olympic final, Courtney led at the start but Sowell soon took over. He led thru 600 metres, the first lap done in 52.8. At 600, four were in contention for medals – Courtney, Sowell, Boysen and Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/69194"} "Derek Johnson"] ". At the top of the stretch, Johnson and Courtney took a slight lead and battled together to the line, with Courtney winning in the lean."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "153"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78270"} "Tom Courtney"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:52.7 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "1:53.6 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:47.7 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "137"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69194"} "Derek Johnson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "1:50.8 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "1:50.2 (3 h2)"] [:td {} "1:47.8 (2)"] [:td {}